The proof has been written to `proof.md`. 

**Summary**: The answer is $\boxed{32}$, obtained via the automorphism orbit argument. The automorphism group $\operatorname{Aut}(\mathbb{R}, \cdot) \cong \operatorname{GL}(\mathbb{R}, \mathbb{Q})$ has exactly 5 orbits on $\mathbb{R}$: $\{0\}$, $\{1\}$, $\{-1\}$, $\mathbb{R}_{>0}\setminus\{1\}$, and $\mathbb{R}_{<0}\setminus\{-1\}$. Each orbit is parameter-free definable, and parameter-free definable sets are exactly unions of orbits, giving $2^5 = 32$ subsets.
